---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="NV Studio Design - Modern Residential Architectural Design"
  description="NV Studio Design showcases contemporary residential architectural masterpieces, featuring sleek lines, innovative design, building permits, and interior design services."
  keywords="architectural design, building permits, interior design, modern architecture, residential design, Toronto architect"
  headerClass="alt"
>
  <section id="one">
    <div class="inner">
      <header class="major">
        <h1>Home</h1>
      </header>

      <!-- Placeholder Content - TO BE REPLACED -->
      <div
        style="background: #fff; color: #333; padding: 2rem; border: 2px dashed #ccc; border-radius: 4px; font-family: monospace; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.8;"
      >
        <p style="color: #e74c3c; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          📋 TODO for Home section
        </p>

        <p><strong>Purpose</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Instantly communicate <em>what you do</em>, <em>for whom</em>, and <em>where</em></li>
          <li>Act as the main SEO authority page (your primary hub)</li>
          <li>Rank for broad, competitive terms: "Residential Architect GTA", "Residential Architecture Studio Toronto", "Custom Home Architect Ontario"</li>
          <li>Establish trust immediately with clear positioning</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>SEO Requirements (CRITICAL)</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>H1 Tag:</strong> Must be "Residential Architecture Studio in the GTA" or similar (ONE H1 only)</li>
          <li><strong>Title Tag:</strong> Max 60 characters. Example: "Residential Architect GTA | NV Studio Design"</li>
          <li><strong>Meta Description:</strong> 150-160 chars for CTR. Example: "Award-winning residential architects in the GTA specializing in custom homes, renovations, and sustainable design. Book a consultation."</li>
          <li><strong>Geographic Keywords:</strong> Must include "GTA", "Greater Toronto Area", "Toronto", "Ontario" naturally in content</li>
          <li><strong>Internal Linking:</strong> Link to Architectural Design, Interior Design, Portfolio, Process, Contact pages</li>
          <li><strong>Content Length:</strong> 600-900 words minimum (not just images)</li>
          <li><strong>Image Alt Text:</strong> Descriptive, include location when relevant. Example: "modern-residential-home-architect-toronto-gta.jpg" not "IMG_1234.jpg"</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Content Structure & Examples</strong></p>

        <p><strong>1. Hero Section (Above the fold)</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>H1:</strong> "Residential Architecture Studio in the GTA"</li>
          <li><strong>Positioning Statement (1-2 sentences):</strong>
            <br/>Example: "Custom homes, renovations, and additions for homeowners and developers across the Greater Toronto Area and Ontario."</li>
          <li><strong>CTA Button:</strong> "Book a Consultation" (links to /contact)</li>
          <li><strong>Note:</strong> No jargon, no philosophy yet. Be direct and clear.</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>2. Who We Serve Section</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Qualify visitors and reduce bad leads</li>
          <li><strong>Example content:</strong>
            <ul>
              <li>Homeowners planning a custom home</li>
              <li>Clients renovating or adding to an existing house</li>
              <li>Developers/builders needing permit-ready drawings</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>3. Services Overview (with internal links)</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Brief intro paragraph mentioning GTA/Ontario focus</li>
          <li>Link cards to:
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Architectural Design</strong> (link to /architectural-design) - "Residential architectural design including zoning, permits, and coordination"</li>
              <li><strong>Interior Design</strong> (link to /interior-design) - "Residential interior design integrated with architectural services"</li>
              <li><strong>Planning & Building Permits</strong> (link to /building-permits) - "Zoning review, feasibility studies, and permit drawings"</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>Each card should have descriptive text (not just titles)</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>4. Featured Projects (2-3 projects)</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Showcase real residential work with context</li>
          <li>Each project card should include:
            <ul>
              <li>High-quality image (optimized, WebP format preferred)</li>
              <li>Project title</li>
              <li>City/area (e.g., "Toronto", "Mississauga", "Oakville")</li>
              <li>Project type (e.g., "Custom Home", "Renovation", "Addition")</li>
              <li>Year (if available)</li>
              <li>Link to full project page</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li><strong>Example project card text:</strong> "Modern Residential Villa | Toronto | Custom Home | 2023"</li>
          <li><strong>SEO Note:</strong> These project links pass authority to individual project pages (critical for long-tail SEO)</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>5. Why Work With Us (Trust Signals)</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Short, factual statements (avoid buzzwords)</li>
          <li><strong>Example content:</strong>
            <ul>
              <li>Residential focus (not commercial)</li>
              <li>Experience with GTA zoning & permits</li>
              <li>Clear communication with builders and developers</li>
              <li>Hands-on studio approach</li>
              <li>Licensed architect (if applicable - OAA, RAIC credentials)</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li><strong>E-E-A-T Signals:</strong> Include credentials, experience, real project examples</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>6. Process Overview (Brief)</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Short 3-5 step overview</li>
          <li><strong>Example:</strong>
            <ol>
              <li>Initial consultation & site review</li>
              <li>Concept & feasibility</li>
              <li>Design development</li>
              <li>Permit drawings & approvals</li>
              <li>Construction coordination</li>
            </ol>
          </li>
          <li>Link to full Process page for details</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>7. Final CTA Section</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Strong closing call-to-action</li>
          <li><strong>Example:</strong> "Planning a residential project in the GTA? Book a consultation to discuss your vision."</li>
          <li>Button: "Book a Consultation" (links to /contact)</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Implementation Notes</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Text is critical:</strong> Never create image-only sections. Every visual must have accompanying descriptive text.</li>
          <li><strong>Performance:</strong> Optimize all images (compress, use WebP, lazy load below fold)</li>
          <li><strong>Internal Links:</strong> Link to Architectural Design, Interior Design, Portfolio, Process, About, Contact pages naturally within content</li>
          <li><strong>Geographic Context:</strong> Mention "GTA", "Greater Toronto Area", "Toronto", "Ontario" naturally throughout (not keyword stuffing)</li>
          <li><strong>Mobile-First:</strong> Ensure all content is readable and functional on mobile devices</li>
          <li><strong>Schema Markup:</strong> Consider adding LocalBusiness schema with address, phone, service area</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>What NOT to Include</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>❌ Long philosophy essays</li>
          <li>❌ Marketing buzzwords ("innovative", "cutting-edge" without context)</li>
          <li>❌ Image-only sections without text</li>
          <li>❌ Generic statements that could apply to any architecture firm</li>
          <li>❌ Overly technical jargon that confuses homeowners</li>
          <li>❌ Separate sections for every micro-service (keep it focused)</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>SEO Keyword Targets (use naturally)</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Primary: "residential architect GTA", "residential architecture studio Toronto", "custom home architect Ontario"</li>
          <li>Secondary: "residential architect Toronto", "GTA architect", "residential design GTA", "home architect Toronto"</li>
          <li>Long-tail: "custom home architect Greater Toronto Area", "residential renovation architect Ontario"</li>
          <li><strong>Important:</strong> Write for humans first, SEO second. Keywords should feel natural in context.</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Content Tone & Style</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Professional, confident, accessible</li>
          <li>Written for non-architects (homeowners and developers)</li>
          <li>Avoid academic or overly technical language</li>
          <li>Be specific about GTA/Ontario focus (not generic "we serve clients everywhere")</li>
          <li>Show, don't just tell (use real project examples)</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Success Metrics</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Visitor should understand in 10 seconds: "This is a residential architecture studio in the GTA"</li>
          <li>Clear path to consultation booking</li>
          <li>Internal links distribute SEO authority to service and project pages</li>
          <li>Page loads in under 3 seconds</li>
          <li>Mobile-friendly and accessible</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

